# DO NOT `cp .env.example .env` — it will not boot. Run this instead:
#
#     ./scripts/bootstrap.sh                 (or: powershell -File scripts\bootstrap.ps1)
#
# which writes .env from this file with the five required secrets generated, and substitutes
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD into DATABASE_URL. Copying this file by hand leaves those five empty, and four
# of them are `:?` guards in docker-compose.yml, so compose refuses before a container exists.
#
# NEVER commit the real .env. Every value left empty below is deliberately empty — a template that
# ships real-looking secrets is how one ends up committed.
#
# Each empty key below says which of the two it is:
#   REQUIRED — the stack refuses to start without it (compose `:?`, or a log.Fatalf at boot)
#   OPTIONAL — the stack boots fine; one named feature stays dark
#
# Generate each one with:  openssl rand -hex 32

PORT=9000
GIN_MODE=

# ── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Port 5432 is intentionally NOT published to the host (see docker-compose.yml):
# this database stores every device's encrypted admin credential.
POSTGRES_USER=postgres
# REQUIRED — compose refuses to start without it, and the same value has to appear inside
# DATABASE_URL below (bootstrap.sh substitutes both).
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
POSTGRES_DB=starter_web
DATABASE_URL=host=postgres port=5432 user=postgres password=<POSTGRES_PASSWORD> dbname=starter_web sslmode=disable

# ── Auth ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED — compose refuses to start, and the server exits at startup, if this is unset.
JWT_SECRET=

# ── Device credential encryption (AES-256-GCM) ──────────────────────────────
# Protects the admin password of every managed firewall. The server refuses to
# start if the ACTIVE version's key is unset, too short, or a known placeholder.
#
# It protects THREE tables, not just the devices:
#   network_devices.password_enc      the shared firewall account
#   device_credentials.password_enc   each person's own firewall account
#   notify_channels.secret_enc        the LINE bot token
#
# Rotating:
#   1. add CRED_ENC_KEY_V<N+1> AND pass it through in docker-compose.yml, then set
#      CRED_ENC_KEY_VERSION=<N+1>. Leave the previous key in place — it is the only
#      thing that can still read rows written before the rotation. Restart the backend.
#   2. POST /admin/rotate-cred-key  (admin only) — re-encrypts all three tables
#   3. check the `tables` object in the response: EVERY table must report
#      failed=0 and rotated+skipped=total. Deleting the old key while one table still
#      holds old-version rows makes those rows unreadable for good, with no error.
#   4. only then remove the previous key from .env and docker-compose.yml
CRED_ENC_KEY_VERSION=1
# REQUIRED — backend/main.go calls platform.ValidateCredKeyConfig() before serving a byte and
# exits on a missing, too-short (<16 chars) or known-placeholder value. There is no fallback on
# purpose: it used to default to a string published in docker-compose.yml.
CRED_ENC_KEY=
# CRED_ENC_KEY_V2=
# CRED_ENC_KEY_V3=

# ── First-boot seeding (all optional) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Read ONCE, by config.SeedDatabase, on a database that has no rows yet. Changing one later does
# nothing — the seed skips any table that is already populated.
#
# The seeded administrator's password (admin@got.co.th — the ONLY account a fresh install gets).
# Unset means the built-in default in backend/config/db.go, which is published with the source and
# announced loudly in the startup log. Set this before the FIRST boot on anything more than one
# person can reach; afterwards it does nothing, because the seed skips a table that has rows.
# A configured value is named in the log but never printed.
# SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
#
# Outgoing mail account used for OTP and report delivery, stored encrypted at rest. If EITHER is
# blank no account is seeded at all and email stays off until one is added from the app — a real
# Gmail app password used to be a literal in config/db.go instead, which encryption cannot help.
# SEED_SMTP_EMAIL=
# SEED_SMTP_APP_PASSWORD=
#
# Password for the sample FortiGate row (10.10.20.90). Unset seeds the placeholder CHANGE_ME,
# which has to be replaced from the web UI before any backup or deploy can run.
# SEED_DEVICE_PASSWORD=

# ── Redis ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The job queue's password. 6379 is not published and Redis sits on the compose
# network only, so this is defence in depth — but the queue is how jobs reach the
# firewalls, so anything else running on this host should not be able to read it.
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# Hex on purpose: the value goes inside a redis:// URL, where a raw : @ / or #
# would have to be percent-encoded. compose refuses to start without it, and the
# redis container must be RECREATED (not restarted) when it changes.
# REQUIRED — compose refuses to start without it.
REDIS_PASSWORD=

# ── Worker callbacks ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shared by the backend and the Python worker; must be IDENTICAL in both.
# It is the only thing guarding /internal/* (job results, deploy outcomes,
# compliance verdicts), so a placeholder value is rejected at startup.
# REQUIRED — compose refuses to start, and platform.ValidateWorkerSecret() exits the backend, if
# this is unset, under 16 chars, or a known placeholder.
WORKER_SHARED_SECRET=

# ── URLs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:9000
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:5173
CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173

# ── Trusted reverse proxies ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated IPs/CIDRs that are allowed to set X-Forwarded-For. Anything else's header is
# ignored and the client IP is the address that actually connected.
#
# Leave BLANK for `go run` / direct access to :9000 — that is the safe default.
# docker compose already passes the nginx container's static /32, so you do not need to set this
# unless you put another proxy (a load balancer, an ingress) in front of the stack: then list that
# proxy instead. Getting it wrong is not silent-safe in one direction — trusting too much lets a
# client forge the header and walk past LoginLimiter and AILimiter.
TRUSTED_PROXIES=

# Only needed if 172.31.240.0/24 collides with another docker network on this host. Both must move
# together: FRONTEND_IP has to sit inside APPNET_SUBNET, and compose derives TRUSTED_PROXIES from it.
# APPNET_SUBNET=172.31.240.0/24
# FRONTEND_IP=172.31.240.10

# ── OAuth (optional — leave blank to disable) ───────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — a pair left blank hides that one sign-in button. Email + password still works, so the
# app is fully usable with all three blank.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
LINE_CLIENT_ID=
LINE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ── AI Assistant (blank = feature off) ──────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — blank boots fine; the AI Assistant page answers "not configured" and every AI wizard
# is unavailable. Nothing else is affected.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Pin the model explicitly — an empty value falls back to a hard-coded default in ai.go,
# which means a redeploy could change which model answers without anyone noticing.
#
# claude-sonnet-5 is both newer and cheaper than the claude-sonnet-4-6 that used to be here
# ($2/$10 per MTok against $3/$15). Whatever you pin, it must support FORCED tool use
# (tool_choice: {type:"tool"}) — the AI Assistant's whole contract is one forced call to
# propose_device_config. Sonnet 5 and Opus 5 do; the Fable/Mythos family returns 400.
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# Audit / Review — whether a qualified assessor has signed off the standards mapping.
# Leave unset for "draft". Set to "reviewed" ONLY on a deployment where that is true:
# the UI drops its "draft mapping" badge and the evidence PDF stops flagging the caveat.
AUDIT_CATALOGUE_STATUS=

# ── Trace Route hop geolocation (optional, offline) ───────────────────────────
# Adds country / city / ASN / ISP to PUBLIC hops on /admin/diagnostics/traceroute, read from local
# MaxMind GeoLite2 databases — no third-party API is ever called. Entirely optional: with no
# databases the hop detail still shows reverse DNS + address-kind + internal-role.
#
# To enable: get a free MaxMind license key (https://www.maxmind.com/en/geolite2/signup), then
#   MAXMIND_LICENSE_KEY=<key> ./scripts/download-geoip.sh
# which drops the .mmdb files into backend/geoip/ (git-ignored, mounted read-only at /geoip).
#
# These paths are the in-container defaults from docker-compose.yml; override only to relocate.
# GEOIP_CITY_DB=/geoip/GeoLite2-City.mmdb
# GEOIP_ASN_DB=/geoip/GeoLite2-ASN.mmdb
